  {
   "id": "s3-21",
   "name": "Algorithmic instructions: input, output, assignment, selection and iteration"
  }
 ],
 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Basic instructions used in pseudocode:\n• INPUT / READ: get data. OUTPUT / PRINT: show results.\n• Assignment: store a value in a variable, e.g. total ← total + mark.\n• Sequence: steps carried out one after another.\n• Selection: IF condition THEN … ELSE … ENDIF chooses between paths.\n• Iteration (loops): FOR i ← 1 TO n … NEXT i (a fixed number of times); WHILE condition DO … ENDWHILE (while a condition is true); REPEAT … UNTIL condition.\nComparison operators: =, <>, <, >, <=, >=.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "learn": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {},
  "sections": [
   {
    "heading": "The building blocks",
    "text": "Every algorithm is made from a few kinds of instruction:\n• Input (INPUT, READ): get data, e.g. INPUT mark.\n• Output (OUTPUT, PRINT): show results.\n• Assignment: store a value in a variable, e.g. total ← total + mark (read the arrow as 'becomes').\n• Sequence: carry out steps in order, one after another."
   },
   {
    "heading": "Selection",
    "text": "Selection lets an algorithm choose. IF condition THEN … ELSE … ENDIF.\nIF mark >= {10} THEN OUTPUT 'Pass' ELSE OUTPUT 'Fail' ENDIF.\nConditions use comparison operators: = (equal), <> (not equal), <, >, <=, >=. Only one branch runs."
   },
   {
    "heading": "Iteration (loops)",
    "text": "Loops repeat steps:\n• FOR i ← {1} TO {5} … NEXT i: repeats a fixed number of times ({5}).\n• WHILE condition DO … ENDWHILE: repeats while the condition is true (it may run zero times).\n• REPEAT … UNTIL condition: runs at least once, until the condition becomes true.\ntotal ← {0}; FOR i ← {1} TO {4}: total ← total + i gives {1} + {2} + {3} + {4} = {10}."
   }
  ],
  "key_words": [
   {
    "word": "assignment",
    "meaning": "storing a value in a variable"
   },
   {
    "word": "selection",
    "meaning": "choosing between paths with IF"
   },
   {
    "word": "iteration",
    "meaning": "repeating steps in a loop"
   },
   {
    "word": "condition",
    "meaning": "a test that is true or false"
   }
  ],
  "examples": [
   "IF x > {0} THEN OUTPUT 'positive'",
   "FOR i ← {1} TO {3}: OUTPUT i",
   "count ← count + {1}"
  ],
  "mistake": {
   "wrong": "FOR i ← {2} TO {5} runs {3} times",
   "right": "It runs {4} times: {2}, {3}, {4}, {5}",
   "why": "Count both the first and last values: last − first + {1}."
  }
 },
